<section class="page-hero"><span class="pub-kicker">Switching to StockChief</span><h1>Bring your records.<br>Review the interpretation.</h1><p>Start with a supported connected system, spreadsheet, document or readable image. StockChief prepares a review before approved records become part of your operation.</p></section><section class="migration-path"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Choose a source</h2><p>Upload a supported file, paste records, connect an import-capable platform or enter items manually. Upload limits and supported formats are shown in the application.</p></div><b>Keep the original</b></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>Review the fields</h2><p>Check interpreted products, SKUs, variants, locations, prices and recognized operational fields. Unclear values may require confirmation.</p></div><b>Visible interpretation</b></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>Answer the required questions</h2><p>Choose stock locations and resolve genuine tracking, currency or matching questions. Missing serial or lot evidence cannot be invented.</p></div><b>Clarify the evidence</b></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>Choose how stock is applied</h2><p>Review the offered update mode, matched records, exclusions and any approved partial import before continuing.</p></div><b>You approve</b></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>Import and verify</h2><p>Follow the saved import progress and verification result. Interrupted work retains its status; review it before retrying so completed work is not repeated.</p></div><b>Saved progress</b></article><article><span>06</span><div><h2>Set up the next part of the business</h2><p>Add supplier and customer records, connections, tax settings and operating authority as needed. Each supported workflow keeps its own approval requirements.</p></div><b>Build on verified records</b></article></section><section class="qualification-note"><h2>Plan the migration around your actual source</h2><p>Readable, structured records are the best starting point. Image quality, missing identifiers, file size, provider permissions and unusual source structures can require clarification. A complete historical cutover of every record type needs a reviewed migration plan.</p><a href="/contact">Email us about a complex migration →</a></section><section class="truth-final"><h2>Start with one<br>understandable source.</h2><div class="pub-actions"><a class="pub-btn" href="/pricing">Choose your plan</a><a class="pub-btn pub-btn--secondary" href="/demo">See the actual application</a></div></section>
